# Claude Context for django-language

## Project Mission
Django language learning app for English, Hungarian, and German. Three learning goals: AI-assisted development, technology stack mastery (Django/Python/Poetry/Docker), and building a practical application.

## Tech Stack
- Django 5.2.8, Python 3.14, Poetry 2.1.3
- Docker (`python:3.14-slim`), SQLite (dev), MIT licensed
- Django i18n for internationalization

## Docker Setup
- **No virtualenvs in containers**: `POETRY_VIRTUALENVS_CREATE=false`
- Use `docker compose` (not `docker-compose`)
- Standard workflow: `docker compose up --build` (first time), then `docker compose up`
- Execute commands: `docker compose exec web python manage.py <command>`

## Poetry
- Modern syntax: use `--without dev`, never deprecated `--no-dev`
- Add deps: `poetry add <pkg>` or `poetry add --group dev <pkg>`
- Local commands: `poetry run python manage.py <command>`

## Code Quality
Tools: Black (formatter), Flake8 (linter), isort (imports), pytest (testing)

Pre-commit: `poetry run black . && poetry run flake8 . && poetry run isort . && poetry run pytest`

## Apps & Models

### vocabulary (Shared vocabulary models)
- `Language`: code (en/hu/de), name, native flag
- `Word`: language FK, text, translation, definition, timestamps

### wod (Word of the Day)
- Uses models from vocabulary app
- Provides random word view functionality

## Key Conventions
- **Static files**: `static/` at root, use `{% load static %}` and `{% static %}` tags
- **i18n**: Use `gettext_lazy` for all user-facing text, support en/hu/de
- **Templates**: Organize by app, use template inheritance
- **Models**: Include timestamps, `__str__` methods, proper FKs

## Common Commands

### Makefile (Recommended)
The project includes a Makefile for simplified commands:
```bash
make help        # Show all available commands
make build       # Build and start (first time)
make up          # Start application (foreground with logs)
make start       # Start application (background/detached)
make down        # Stop application
make test        # Run tests
make shell       # Django shell
make migrate     # Run migrations
make format      # Format code (black + isort)
make lint        # Run flake8
```

### Docker (Direct)
```bash
docker compose up --build    # First run
docker compose up            # Normal start
docker compose exec web python manage.py migrate
docker compose exec web python manage.py createsuperuser
docker compose exec web pytest
```

### Database
```bash
makemigrations [app]  # Create migrations
migrate               # Apply migrations
shell                 # Django shell
```

## GitHub Config
- Main branch: `main`, auto-delete branches on PR merge
- 15 commits, 2 contributors

## Claude Guidelines
- **Style**: Concise but educational, minimal formatting unless requested
- **Approach**: Docker-first, modern Poetry syntax, suggest tests/linting
- **Consider**: i18n, security, performance, Django best practices

